JobParametersValidator: 
JobParametersValidator is an interface in Spring Batch that allows you to validate the job parameters provided at the time of job execution. 
It provides a way to ensure that the input parameters passed to a job are valid and meet certain criteria. 
When you implement this interface, you can define custom validation logic to check if the job parameters are correct.
If the validation fails, an exception is thrown, and the job execution is aborted. 
The JobParametersValidator is typically used before the job starts, during the job parameter validation phase, 
to ensure that the input parameters are valid before proceeding with the execution.



